  "summary": "Keyword co-occurrence in orchestrator/SDK modules; no exfiltration path traced",
  "details": "Static keyword matches fired on files whose names and contents align with a room/server orchestration SDK: bin/room-orchestrator-boot.js contains curl/POST tokens consistent with bootstrap HTTP calls, and src/sdk/RoomOrchestrator.js, src/sdk/ServerAPI.js, and src/sharding/RegionRouter.js contain 'ping' and HTTP verb tokens consistent with health checks and API calls. The pattern matches are on generic HTTP/health-check primitives (curl, ping, GET, POST) with no named installer-side secret being read (no ~/.aws, ~/.ssh, ~/.npmrc, env-var scraping) and no hardcoded attacker-controlled destination cited in evidence. The co-occurrence of curl + POST or ping + GET is the ordinary shape of an SDK's networking layer, not by itself evidence of exfiltration.",
